    "title": "Wild pig hunting season beginning at Solano County wetland - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ken Allard ,\n3 hours ago (FOX40.COM) — Recreational hunters will have the opportunity to help control the wild pig population in a Solano County wetland spanning more than 2,000 acres this spring. Officials with the California Department of Fish and Wildlife announced it is offering wild pig hunting opportunities at Joice Island of the Grizzly Island Wildlife Area. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
